From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDK-BPI EasyMesh Investigation <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 22:38:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi_hal_send_mgmt_frame: use the validated MLO link id

The management-frame transmit path initializes link_id to zero and changes it
to not-applicable only when wifi_hal_is_mld_enabled() is false.  A VAP whose
data model enables MLO but which has no established MLO link therefore emits
NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINK_ID=0.  The kernel rejects the frame with -EINVAL.

Use wifi_hal_get_mld_link_id(), like the other management-frame paths.  The
accessor returns the established link id and, with the existing layer fix,
maps the data model's unset value to NL80211_DRV_LINK_ID_NA.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 wifi_hal.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/wifi_hal.c b/wifi_hal.c
index 1b68868..c812f1e 100644
--- a/wifi_hal.c
+++ b/wifi_hal.c
@@ -4710,8 +4710,5 @@ int wifi_hal_send_mgmt_frame(int apIndex,mac_address_t sta, const unsigned char
 #ifdef HOSTAPD_2_11 // 2.11
-    // Action frames will get rejected by kernel if we pass a valid link_id for non-MLO case.
-    if(!wifi_hal_is_mld_enabled(interface)) {
-        link_id = -1;
-    }
+    link_id = wifi_hal_get_mld_link_id(interface);
     res = wifi_drv_send_mlme(interface, buf, 24 + data_len, 1, freq, NULL, 0, 0, wait, link_id);
 #elif HOSTAPD_2_10 // 2.10
     res = wifi_drv_send_mlme(interface, buf, 24 + data_len, 1, freq, NULL, 0, 0, wait);
